convertKeyToPath.description:
If the key in the default data mapping has a dot or braces, it will be converted into an object. For example:

{ 'a.b': '123' }

After data mapping, it becomes { a: { b: '123 } }

If you want to turn off this function, please set convertKeyToPath to false

advancedSettings.description:
Custom details configuration panel such as: 

{ boolean: [ {type: "input-text", name: "aa", label: "AA" }   ] }

When configuring boolean field details, the above configuration will appear

